# BOXING

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

This document defines the physiological, biomechanical, technical and tactical demands of Boxing.

Its objective is to enable the Combat Athlete System (CAS) to understand what determines boxing performance and how physical preparation should support it.

This document describes performance requirements.

It does not prescribe training methods.

---

# Definition

Boxing is a striking combat sport in which athletes score by delivering punches while avoiding being struck.

Success depends upon:

Technical superiority.

Tactical superiority.

Physical superiority.

Psychological control.

Efficient movement.

---

# Philosophy

Boxing is a sport of controlled violence.

Power matters.

Speed matters.

Endurance matters.

None are sufficient alone.

Elite performance emerges from the interaction between movement efficiency, timing, precision and decision-making.

The objective is not to throw more punches.

The objective is to land the right punch at the right moment.

